# No PRIVATE key ever belongs in this repo, and since sealing moved to phoenix-release-tooling
# there is no key in this repo's CI either: it holds a dispatch token that can ask that repository
# for a signature and nothing else. So there is no keyfile to commit by accident — and this is the
# net under that rule, not the rule itself.
*.key

# Build outputs. mirrors.json is GENERATED from mirrors.d/ at publish time and only ever exists as
# a release asset; a copy committed here would be a second answer to "what is published", free to
# disagree with the signed one.
/mirrors.json
/mirrors.json.minisig

# Bytecode from running the selftest.
__pycache__/
